import Wikipedia.HopfProblem.SingularCohomologyCupClasses

/-!
# Native integral singular cup products

The Alexander--Whitney product is defined by the front and back faces of
actual singular simplices.  Its all-degree Leibniz identity supplies the
genuine coboundary primitives needed for descent to the actual integral
singular-cohomology objects.  The descended bilinear operation is natural
under the original continuous-map pullbacks, and its evaluation on actual
cycles is the original cochain evaluation.

This package constructs the cup operation and its stated properties; it
does not replace native cohomology by a transported exterior-algebra ring.
-/
